{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChPR8bxq12NrcQwQMmZcq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I routed issue #317 as ready to plan and wrote the result to `.ard/317/triage-lead.md`. It goes to the `engineer` triage role for the plan and the `engineer` worker for the code.\n\n- **Why only these two roles:** they are the only triage and worker roles this repository has. The change is a new internal package for talking to Kubernetes (API types, a client interface, an in-cluster connection and a fake for tests).\n- **Not blocked:** the issue depends on #313, #314 and #315. Recent commits show parts 2, 3 and 4 of the Kubernetes executor are already on main, including the one for #315 (#382).\n- **No review entries:** `.ard/config.yaml` gives `eng-review` no `when:` rule, so it runs on every pull request anyway.\n\nThe file also lists three open issues for a maintainer:\n1. **The scope is unclear.** The issue body describes the whole executor. The newest comment cuts part 6A down to the API layer only, so I told the engineer to plan just that.\n2. **Part of the older plan in the comments is out of date.** Design revision 3 replaces whatever that plan says about the job API, the key table, the input tarball and TLS.\n3. **Two design questions are still open:** whether upload runs as a native sidecar or a plain container, and how the credential reaches the pod. They belong to the later executor part. There is no architect role here, so a person needs to answer them before that part is routed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":896,"cache_read_input_tokens":22850,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":896},"output_tokens":470,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"par